<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="nc-que-es">What it means</h3>
  <p>
    When the contract ends, the employer gives you a proposed settlement statement (documento de
    liquidación) with the amounts due to you (art. 49.2 ET). Some people, when they do not agree
    with an amount, sign it adding «recibí no conforme» (received, not agreed) or «no conforme» (not
    agreed).
  </p>
  <p>
    That note does not change what the employer pays you: it puts in writing that you do not agree
    with some figure. We give this only as information. What to do in your case can be assessed by
    an employment law firm, a graduado social (labour relations adviser) office or a trade union.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>49.2</span> ET
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="nc-representante">With someone from the workforce present</h3>
  <p>
    You can ask for a workers’ legal representative to be present when you go to sign the final
    settlement (finiquito). The document records whether you sign it in their presence or have not
    used that option (art. 49.2 ET).
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>49.2</span> ET
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="nc-ejemplo">Example: comparing before signing</h3>
  <p>
    A person earning 1.500&nbsp;€ gross a month with two extra payments of 1.500&nbsp;€ resigns on
    15 October 2026, having worked since 1 March 2023. They have taken 10 of their 22 working days
    of holiday and have given the 15 days’ notice set by their collective agreement. The proposal
    pays them {euros(OFFERED_HOLIDAYS)} for holiday.
  </p>
  <p class="example">
    <span class="example__label">Holiday</span> The legal minimum comes to {euroRange(range)},
    depending on whether it is counted by days or by months. At least {euros(holidays.difference)}{' '}
    is missing compared with {euros(OFFERED_HOLIDAYS)}.
  </p>
  <p>
    The calculator does the same with each item: enter what the proposal says on the “Your final
    settlement” sheet and you will see what matches the legal minimum and what does not.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="nc-plazos">The time limits keep running</h3>
  <p>
    For outstanding pay, holiday, extra payments or severance pay at the end of a fixed-term
    contract, the time limit is one year (art. 59.1 ET).
  </p>
  <p>
    In a dismissal, the time limit to challenge it is 20 business days (días hábiles) (art. 59.3
    ET). That time limit is interrupted when you file the request for conciliation with the relevant
    public mediation, arbitration and conciliation service. It is short, and an employment law firm,
    a graduado social (labour relations adviser) office or a trade union can tell you which one
    applies to your case.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>59</span> ET
  </p>
</section>
